{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GSfaLtXvJF47TeeipJt2VA","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Now let me create a comprehensive summary of the full contents:\n\n## Complete Playwright Demo Infrastructure Report\n\nI've thoroughly explored the Playwright demo infrastructure. Here's the complete breakdown of all files:\n\n---\n\n### 1. **docs/demos/helpers/code-server.ts**\nLaunches and manages code-server instances:\n- `REPO_ROOT`, `DEMO_WORKSPACE`, `DEFAULT_PORT` constants\n- `codeServerURL()` - get base URL (respects `CODE_SERVER_URL` env var)\n- `vsixPath()` - path to packaged VSIX extension\n- `waitForPort()` - TCP port polling with 30s timeout\n- `installExtension()` - runs `code-server --install-extension` separately (must exit before server launch)\n- `launchCodeServer()` - main launch function:\n  - Installs extension first (unless `skipExtensionInstall` is true)\n  - Spawns code-server with args: `--port`, `--auth none`, `--disable-telemetry`, `--disable-update-check`, `--disable-workspace-trust`, `--disable-getting-started-override`, and workspace path\n  - Sets PATH to include smelt LSP binary from `target/debug`\n  - Logs stderr if DEBUG env var set\n  - Returns `CodeServerHandle` with `process`, `url`, `port`, `stop()` method\n\n---\n\n### 2. **docs/demos/helpers/editor.ts**\nHigh-level VS Code editor interaction helpers for Playwright:\n\n**Dialog/Initialization:**\n- `dismissDialogs()` - closes trust prompt, welcome tab, any overlays\n- `waitForWorkbench()` - waits for `.monaco-workbench` and `.editor-instance`\n- `waitForLSPReady()` - waits 3s baseline, then polls for diagnostics (`.squiggly-error` or `.squiggly-warning`)\n\n**File Navigation:**\n- `openFile(filePath)` - Ctrl+P quick-open, type path, Enter\n- `goToLine(line)` - Ctrl+G, type line number, Enter\n- `getActiveTabName()` - returns current tab's label\n\n**Text Editing:**\n- `typeText(text)` - type with 50ms delay between chars\n- `selectAll()` - Ctrl+A\n\n**LSP Features:**\n- `hoverWord(word, opts?)` - finds word span, hovers, waits for `.monaco-hover-content`\n- `triggerCompletion()` - Ctrl+Space, waits for `.editor-widget.suggest-widget`\n- `goToDefinition()` - F12, 1.5s wait\n- `findReferences()` - Shift+F12, waits for `.reference-zone-widget` or `.references-view`\n- `rename(newName)` - F2, types name, Enter, 1s wait\n- `getCodeActions()` - Ctrl+., waits for action widget\n- `waitForDiagnostics(opts?)` - waits for `.squiggly-error`, `.squiggly-warning`, or `.squiggly-info` (default 30s timeout)\n\n---\n\n### 3. **docs/demos/helpers/capture.ts**\nScreenshot and media management:\n- `MEDIA_DIR` - resolves to `docs/demos/media`\n- `mediaDir(feature)` - creates `MEDIA_DIR/<feature>` and returns path\n- `screenshot(page, opts)` - saves to `media/<feature>/<name>.png`, supports clip and fullPage options\n- `screenshotEditor(page, opts)` - captures `.editor-container` only, fallback to full page\n- `screenshotWithOverlay(page, opts)` - full-page screenshot to capture overlays\n\n---\n\n### 4. **docs/demos/tests/smoke.spec.ts**\nSmoke test suite (3 tests):\n\n**Setup:**\n- `beforeAll`: launches code-server (unless `CODE_SERVER_URL` env var is set)\n- `afterAll`: stops server\n\n**Tests:**\n1. **\"code-server loads the demo workspace\"**\n   - Navigate to server URL\n   - Wait for workbench, dismiss dialogs\n   - Assert workbench is visible\n   - Screenshot: `smoke/workbench-loaded.png`\n\n2. **\"smelt extension activates and produces diagnostics\"**\n   - Navigate, wait, dismiss dialogs\n   - Open `bad_ref.sql` (has typo in smelt.ref())\n   - Wait for diagnostics (45s timeout)\n   - Assert error count > 0\n   - Screenshot: `smoke/diagnostics-active.png`\n\n3. **\"clean model has no errors\"**\n   - Navigate, wait, dismiss dialogs\n   - Open `stg_users.sql`\n   - Wait 5s for LSP\n   - Assert error count == 0\n   - Screenshot: `smoke/clean-model.png`\n\n---\n\n### 5. **docs/demos/playwright.config.ts**\nPlaywright configuration:\n- `testDir: \"./tests\"`\n- `timeout: 120_000` (2 min per test)\n- `retries: 0`, `workers: 1` (serial execution)\n- `reporter: [[\"list\"], [\"html\", { open: \"never\" }]]`\n- `use`:\n  - `baseURL: CODE_SERVER_URL ?? \"http://localhost:18080\"`\n  - `viewport: { width: 1280, height: 720 }`\n  - `video: \"on\"`, `screenshot: \"on\"`, `trace: \"retain-on-failure\"`\n  - `navigationTimeout: 30_000`, `actionTimeout: 15_000`\n- `outputDir: \"./test-results\"`\n\n---\n\n### 6. **docs/demos/package.json**\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"smelt-lsp-demos\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"description\": \"Playwright-driven LSP feature demos for smelt documentation\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"test\": \"playwright test\",\n    \"test:smoke\": \"playwright test tests/smoke.spec.ts\",\n    \"start-server\": \"bash scripts/start-code-server.sh\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@playwright/test\": \"^1.52.0\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 7. **examples/demo_workspace/** (file listing)\n```\nexamples/demo_workspace/\n├── .vscode/\n│   └── settings.json\n├── models/\n│   ├── broken/\n│   │   ├── bad_ref.sql\n│   │   ├── type_mismatch.sql\n│   │   └── missing_column.sql\n│   ├── intermediate/\n│   │   ├── user_first_purchase.sql\n│   │   └── user_sessions.sql\n│   ├── marts/\n│   │   ├── daily_revenue.sql\n│   │   └── user_lifetime_value.sql\n│   └── staging/\n│       ├── stg_users.sql\n│       └── stg_events.sql\n├── smelt.yml\n└── sources.yml\n```\n\n---\n\n### 8. **examples/demo_workspace/models/broken/bad_ref.sql**\n```sql\n-- Model with a typo in the ref call\nSELECT\n    user_id,\n    email\nFROM smelt.ref('stg_uusers')\n```\nIntentional error: typo `stg_uusers` instead of `stg_users`\n\n---\n\n### 9. **examples/demo_workspace/models/broken/type_mismatch.sql**\n```sql\n-- Model with a type mismatch: comparing INTEGER user_id to a string\nSELECT\n    user_id,\n    email\nFROM smelt.ref('stg_users')\nWHERE user_id = 'abc'\n```\nIntentional error: comparing INTEGER to string literal\n\n---\n\n### 10. **examples/demo_workspace/models/broken/missing_column.sql**\n```sql\n-- Model referencing a column that does not exist upstream\nSELECT\n    user_id,\n    nonexistent_col\nFROM smelt.ref('stg_users')\n```\nIntentional error: `nonexistent_col` doesn't exist in stg_users\n\n---\n\n### 11. **examples/demo_workspace/models/marts/daily_revenue.sql**\n```sql\n-- Daily revenue rollup from events\nSELECT\n    DATE_TRUNC('day', event_time) AS revenue_date,\n    COUNT(DISTINCT user_id) AS paying_users,\n    SUM(revenue_cents) AS total_revenue_cents\nFROM smelt.ref('stg_events')\nWHERE event_type = 'purchase'\nGROUP BY revenue_date\n```\n\n---\n\n### 12. **examples/demo_workspace/models/marts/user_lifetime_value.sql**\n```sql\n-- Lifetime value per user combining sessions and first purchase\nSELECT\n    s.user_id,\n    fp.email,\n    fp.plan_type,\n    fp.first_purchase_time,\n    COUNT(DISTINCT s.session_date) AS total_active_days,\n    SUM(s.session_revenue_cents) AS lifetime_revenue_cents\nFROM smelt.ref('user_sessions') AS s\nLEFT JOIN smelt.ref('user_first_purchase') AS fp ON s.user_id = fp.user_id\nGROUP BY s.user_id, fp.email, fp.plan_type, fp.first_purchase_time\n```\n\n---\n\n### 13. **examples/demo_workspace/models/intermediate/user_first_purchase.sql**\n```sql\n-- First purchase event per user\nWITH purchases AS (\n    SELECT\n        e.user_id,\n        e.event_time AS purchase_time,\n        e.revenue_cents,\n        ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY e.user_id ORDER BY e.event_time) AS rn\n    FROM smelt.ref('stg_events') AS e\n    WHERE e.event_type = 'purchase'\n)\nSELECT\n    p.user_id,\n    u.email,\n    u.plan_type,\n    p.purchase_time AS first_purchase_time,\n    p.revenue_cents AS first_purchase_cents\nFROM purchases AS p\nINNER JOIN smelt.ref('stg_users') AS u ON p.user_id = u.user_id\nWHERE p.rn = 1\n```\n\n---\n\n### 14. **examples/demo_workspace/models/intermediate/user_sessions.sql**\n```sql\n-- Sessionized events grouped by user and day\nSELECT\n    user_id,\n    DATE_TRUNC('day', event_time) AS session_date,\n    COUNT(*) AS event_count,\n    SUM(revenue_cents) AS session_revenue_cents\nFROM smelt.ref('stg_events')\nGROUP BY user_id, session_date\n```\n\n---\n\n### 15. **examples/demo_workspace/models/staging/stg_users.sql**\n```sql\n-- Cleaned user data from raw source\nSELECT\n    user_id,\n    LOWER(email) AS email,\n    signup_date,\n    plan_type\nFROM smelt.source('raw.users')\n```\n\n---\n\n### 16. **examples/demo_workspace/models/staging/stg_events.sql**\n```sql\n-- Cleaned event stream with revenue in dollars\nSELECT\n    event_id,\n    user_id,\n    event_type,\n    event_time,\n    revenue_cents\nFROM smelt.source('raw.events')\n```\n\n---\n\n### 17. **examples/demo_workspace/sources.yml**\n```yaml\nversion: 1\n\nsources:\n  raw:\n    tables:\n      users:\n        description: \"Raw user data from the application database\"\n        columns:\n          - name: user_id\n            type: INTEGER\n            description: \"Unique user identifier\"\n          - name: email\n            type: VARCHAR\n            description: \"User email address\"\n          - name: signup_date\n            type: DATE\n            description: \"Date the user signed up\"\n          - name: plan_type\n            type: VARCHAR\n            description: \"Subscription plan (free, pro, enterprise)\"\n      events:\n        description: \"Raw event stream from the application\"\n        columns:\n          - name: event_id\n            type: INTEGER\n            description: \"Unique event identifier\"\n          - name: user_id\n            type: INTEGER\n            description: \"User who triggered the event\"\n          - name: event_type\n            type: VARCHAR\n            description: \"Type of event (page_view, purchase, signup)\"\n          - name: event_time\n            type: TIMESTAMP\n            description: \"When the event occurred\"\n          - name: revenue_cents\n            type: INTEGER\n            description: \"Revenue in cents (for purchase events)\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### 18. **examples/demo_workspace/smelt.yml**\n```yaml\nname: demo_workspace\nversion: 1\n\nmodel_paths:\n  - models\n\ntargets:\n  dev:\n    type: duckdb\n    database: target/dev.duckdb\n    schema: main\n\ndefault_materialization: view\n\nmodels:\n  stg_users:\n    materialization: table\n  stg_events:\n    materialization: table\n```\n\n---\n\n### 19. **examples/demo_workspace/.vscode/settings.json**\n```json\n{\n  \"smelt.trace.server\": \"verbose\",\n  \"files.associations\": {\n    \"*.sql\": \"smelt\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Key Patterns for Writing New Tests\n\n**Pattern 1: Basic test structure**\n```typescript\nlet server: CodeServerHandle;\n\ntest.beforeAll(async () => {\n  if (!process.env.CODE_SERVER_URL) {\n    server = await launchCodeServer();\n  }\n});\n\ntest.afterAll(async () => {\n  server?.stop();\n});\n\ntest(\"description\", async ({ page }) => {\n  const url = process.env.CODE_SERVER_URL ?? server.url;\n  await page.goto(url, { waitUntil: \"load\" });\n  await waitForWorkbench(page);\n  await dismissDialogs(page);\n  // Test logic...\n});\n```\n\n**Pattern 2: Wait for LSP initialization**\n- Use `waitForLSPReady(page, { timeout })` for reliable LSP detection\n- Or `waitForDiagnostics(page, { timeout })` if LSP produces errors on a known-broken file\n\n**Pattern 3: Interact with editor**\n- `openFile(page, \"path/to/file.sql\")` - opens via Ctrl+P\n- `goToLine(page, N)` - positions cursor\n- `hoverWord(page, \"word\", { line })` - triggers hover\n\n**Pattern 4: Screenshot for documentation**\n- `screenshot(page, { feature: \"name\", name: \"step\" })` - saves to `docs/demos/media/name/step.png`\n- `screenshotEditor()` - just editor area, better for tight docs\n- `screenshotWithOverlay()` - captures hover/menu overlays\n\n**Pattern 5: Assert LSP behavior**\n- Count squigglies: `page.locator(\".squiggly-error\").count()`\n- Check specific diagnostics via hover widget content\n\nAll files are ready for you to write new tests following these exact patterns!"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0b24cd0-9bf2-46e1-9f76-5a7eac82855a","uuid":"aeb6b3d8-011e-4d76-a608-777c07ec94cd","timestamp":"2026-04-06T04:46:35.564Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to understand the existing Playwright demo infrastructure for an LSP visual docs project. Please explore thoroughly:\n\n1. Read docs/demos/helpers/code-server.ts, docs/demos/helpers/editor.ts, docs/demos/helpers/capture.ts\n2. Read docs/demos/tests/smoke.spec.ts\n3. Read docs/demos/playwright.config.ts\n4. Read docs/demos/package.json\n5. List files in examples/demo_workspace/ recursively\n6. Read the broken model files: examples/demo_workspace/models/broken/bad_ref.sql, type_mismatch.sql, missing_column.sql\n7. Read examples/demo_workspace/models/marts/daily_revenue.sql and user_lifetime_value.sql\n\nReport the full contents of all these files - I need to see the exact code to write new tests following the same patterns.","agentId":"a4179ffaeb020ae97","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Now let me create a comprehensive summary of the full contents:\n\n## Complete Playwright Demo Infrastructure Report\n\nI've thoroughly explored the Playwright demo infrastructure. Here's the complete breakdown of all files:\n\n---\n\n### 1. **docs/demos/helpers/code-server.ts**\nLaunches and manages code-server instances:\n- `REPO_ROOT`, `DEMO_WORKSPACE`, `DEFAULT_PORT` constants\n- `codeServerURL()` - get base URL (respects `CODE_SERVER_URL` env var)\n- `vsixPath()` - path to packaged VSIX extension\n- `waitForPort()` - TCP port polling with 30s timeout\n- `installExtension()` - runs `code-server --install-extension` separately (must exit before server launch)\n- `launchCodeServer()` - main launch function:\n  - Installs extension first (unless `skipExtensionInstall` is true)\n  - Spawns code-server with args: `--port`, `--auth none`, `--disable-telemetry`, `--disable-update-check`, `--disable-workspace-trust`, `--disable-getting-started-override`, and workspace path\n  - Sets PATH to include smelt LSP binary from `target/debug`\n  - Logs stderr if DEBUG env var set\n  - Returns `CodeServerHandle` with `process`, `url`, `port`, `stop()` method\n\n---\n\n### 2. **docs/demos/helpers/editor.ts**\nHigh-level VS Code editor interaction helpers for Playwright:\n\n**Dialog/Initialization:**\n- `dismissDialogs()` - closes trust prompt, welcome tab, any overlays\n- `waitForWorkbench()` - waits for `.monaco-workbench` and `.editor-instance`\n- `waitForLSPReady()` - waits 3s baseline, then polls for diagnostics (`.squiggly-error` or `.squiggly-warning`)\n\n**File Navigation:**\n- `openFile(filePath)` - Ctrl+P quick-open, type path, Enter\n- `goToLine(line)` - Ctrl+G, type line number, Enter\n- `getActiveTabName()` - returns current tab's label\n\n**Text Editing:**\n- `typeText(text)` - type with 50ms delay between chars\n- `selectAll()` - Ctrl+A\n\n**LSP Features:**\n- `hoverWord(word, opts?)` - finds word span, hovers, waits for `.monaco-hover-content`\n- `triggerCompletion()` - Ctrl+Space, waits for `.editor-widget.suggest-widget`\n- `goToDefinition()` - F12, 1.5s wait\n- `findReferences()` - Shift+F12, waits for `.reference-zone-widget` or `.references-view`\n- `rename(newName)` - F2, types name, Enter, 1s wait\n- `getCodeActions()` - Ctrl+., waits for action widget\n- `waitForDiagnostics(opts?)` - waits for `.squiggly-error`, `.squiggly-warning`, or `.squiggly-info` (default 30s timeout)\n\n---\n\n### 3. **docs/demos/helpers/capture.ts**\nScreenshot and media management:\n- `MEDIA_DIR` - resolves to `docs/demos/media`\n- `mediaDir(feature)` - creates `MEDIA_DIR/<feature>` and returns path\n- `screenshot(page, opts)` - saves to `media/<feature>/<name>.png`, supports clip and fullPage options\n- `screenshotEditor(page, opts)` - captures `.editor-container` only, fallback to full page\n- `screenshotWithOverlay(page, opts)` - full-page screenshot to capture overlays\n\n---\n\n### 4. **docs/demos/tests/smoke.spec.ts**\nSmoke test suite (3 tests):\n\n**Setup:**\n- `beforeAll`: launches code-server (unless `CODE_SERVER_URL` env var is set)\n- `afterAll`: stops server\n\n**Tests:**\n1. **\"code-server loads the demo workspace\"**\n   - Navigate to server URL\n   - Wait for workbench, dismiss dialogs\n   - Assert workbench is visible\n   - Screenshot: `smoke/workbench-loaded.png`\n\n2. **\"smelt extension activates and produces diagnostics\"**\n   - Navigate, wait, dismiss dialogs\n   - Open `bad_ref.sql` (has typo in smelt.ref())\n   - Wait for diagnostics (45s timeout)\n   - Assert error count > 0\n   - Screenshot: `smoke/diagnostics-active.png`\n\n3. **\"clean model has no errors\"**\n   - Navigate, wait, dismiss dialogs\n   - Open `stg_users.sql`\n   - Wait 5s for LSP\n   - Assert error count == 0\n   - Screenshot: `smoke/clean-model.png`\n\n---\n\n### 5. **docs/demos/playwright.config.ts**\nPlaywright configuration:\n- `testDir: \"./tests\"`\n- `timeout: 120_000` (2 min per test)\n- `retries: 0`, `workers: 1` (serial execution)\n- `reporter: [[\"list\"], [\"html\", { open: \"never\" }]]`\n- `use`:\n  - `baseURL: CODE_SERVER_URL ?? \"http://localhost:18080\"`\n  - `viewport: { width: 1280, height: 720 }`\n  - `video: \"on\"`, `screenshot: \"on\"`, `trace: \"retain-on-failure\"`\n  - `navigationTimeout: 30_000`, `actionTimeout: 15_000`\n- `outputDir: \"./test-results\"`\n\n---\n\n### 6. **docs/demos/package.json**\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"smelt-lsp-demos\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"description\": \"Playwright-driven LSP feature demos for smelt documentation\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"test\": \"playwright test\",\n    \"test:smoke\": \"playwright test tests/smoke.spec.ts\",\n    \"start-server\": \"bash scripts/start-code-server.sh\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@playwright/test\": \"^1.52.0\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 7. **examples/demo_workspace/** (file listing)\n```\nexamples/demo_workspace/\n├── .vscode/\n│   └── settings.json\n├── models/\n│   ├── broken/\n│   │   ├── bad_ref.sql\n│   │   ├── type_mismatch.sql\n│   │   └── missing_column.sql\n│   ├── intermediate/\n│   │   ├── user_first_purchase.sql\n│   │   └── user_sessions.sql\n│   ├── marts/\n│   │   ├── daily_revenue.sql\n│   │   └── user_lifetime_value.sql\n│   └── staging/\n│       ├── stg_users.sql\n│       └── stg_events.sql\n├── smelt.yml\n└── sources.yml\n```\n\n---\n\n### 8. **examples/demo_workspace/models/broken/bad_ref.sql**\n```sql\n-- Model with a typo in the ref call\nSELECT\n    user_id,\n    email\nFROM smelt.ref('stg_uusers')\n```\nIntentional error: typo `stg_uusers` instead of `stg_users`\n\n---\n\n### 9. **examples/demo_workspace/models/broken/type_mismatch.sql**\n```sql\n-- Model with a type mismatch: comparing INTEGER user_id to a string\nSELECT\n    user_id,\n    email\nFROM smelt.ref('stg_users')\nWHERE user_id = 'abc'\n```\nIntentional error: comparing INTEGER to string literal\n\n---\n\n### 10. **examples/demo_workspace/models/broken/missing_column.sql**\n```sql\n-- Model referencing a column that does not exist upstream\nSELECT\n    user_id,\n    nonexistent_col\nFROM smelt.ref('stg_users')\n```\nIntentional error: `nonexistent_col` doesn't exist in stg_users\n\n---\n\n### 11. **examples/demo_workspace/models/marts/daily_revenue.sql**\n```sql\n-- Daily revenue rollup from events\nSELECT\n    DATE_TRUNC('day', event_time) AS revenue_date,\n    COUNT(DISTINCT user_id) AS paying_users,\n    SUM(revenue_cents) AS total_revenue_cents\nFROM smelt.ref('stg_events')\nWHERE event_type = 'purchase'\nGROUP BY revenue_date\n```\n\n---\n\n### 12. **examples/demo_workspace/models/marts/user_lifetime_value.sql**\n```sql\n-- Lifetime value per user combining sessions and first purchase\nSELECT\n    s.user_id,\n    fp.email,\n    fp.plan_type,\n    fp.first_purchase_time,\n    COUNT(DISTINCT s.session_date) AS total_active_days,\n    SUM(s.session_revenue_cents) AS lifetime_revenue_cents\nFROM smelt.ref('user_sessions') AS s\nLEFT JOIN smelt.ref('user_first_purchase') AS fp ON s.user_id = fp.user_id\nGROUP BY s.user_id, fp.email, fp.plan_type, fp.first_purchase_time\n```\n\n---\n\n### 13. **examples/demo_workspace/models/intermediate/user_first_purchase.sql**\n```sql\n-- First purchase event per user\nWITH purchases AS (\n    SELECT\n        e.user_id,\n        e.event_time AS purchase_time,\n        e.revenue_cents,\n        ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY e.user_id ORDER BY e.event_time) AS rn\n    FROM smelt.ref('stg_events') AS e\n    WHERE e.event_type = 'purchase'\n)\nSELECT\n    p.user_id,\n    u.email,\n    u.plan_type,\n    p.purchase_time AS first_purchase_time,\n    p.revenue_cents AS first_purchase_cents\nFROM purchases AS p\nINNER JOIN smelt.ref('stg_users') AS u ON p.user_id = u.user_id\nWHERE p.rn = 1\n```\n\n---\n\n### 14. **examples/demo_workspace/models/intermediate/user_sessions.sql**\n```sql\n-- Sessionized events grouped by user and day\nSELECT\n    user_id,\n    DATE_TRUNC('day', event_time) AS session_date,\n    COUNT(*) AS event_count,\n    SUM(revenue_cents) AS session_revenue_cents\nFROM smelt.ref('stg_events')\nGROUP BY user_id, session_date\n```\n\n---\n\n### 15. **examples/demo_workspace/models/staging/stg_users.sql**\n```sql\n-- Cleaned user data from raw source\nSELECT\n    user_id,\n    LOWER(email) AS email,\n    signup_date,\n    plan_type\nFROM smelt.source('raw.users')\n```\n\n---\n\n### 16. **examples/demo_workspace/models/staging/stg_events.sql**\n```sql\n-- Cleaned event stream with revenue in dollars\nSELECT\n    event_id,\n    user_id,\n    event_type,\n    event_time,\n    revenue_cents\nFROM smelt.source('raw.events')\n```\n\n---\n\n### 17. **examples/demo_workspace/sources.yml**\n```yaml\nversion: 1\n\nsources:\n  raw:\n    tables:\n      users:\n        description: \"Raw user data from the application database\"\n        columns:\n          - name: user_id\n            type: INTEGER\n            description: \"Unique user identifier\"\n          - name: email\n            type: VARCHAR\n            description: \"User email address\"\n          - name: signup_date\n            type: DATE\n            description: \"Date the user signed up\"\n          - name: plan_type\n            type: VARCHAR\n            description: \"Subscription plan (free, pro, enterprise)\"\n      events:\n        description: \"Raw event stream from the application\"\n        columns:\n          - name: event_id\n            type: INTEGER\n            description: \"Unique event identifier\"\n          - name: user_id\n            type: INTEGER\n            description: \"User who triggered the event\"\n          - name: event_type\n            type: VARCHAR\n            description: \"Type of event (page_view, purchase, signup)\"\n          - name: event_time\n            type: TIMESTAMP\n            description: \"When the event occurred\"\n          - name: revenue_cents\n            type: INTEGER\n            description: \"Revenue in cents (for purchase events)\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### 18. **examples/demo_workspace/smelt.yml**\n```yaml\nname: demo_workspace\nversion: 1\n\nmodel_paths:\n  - models\n\ntargets:\n  dev:\n    type: duckdb\n    database: target/dev.duckdb\n    schema: main\n\ndefault_materialization: view\n\nmodels:\n  stg_users:\n    materialization: table\n  stg_events:\n    materialization: table\n```\n\n---\n\n### 19. **examples/demo_workspace/.vscode/settings.json**\n```json\n{\n  \"smelt.trace.server\": \"verbose\",\n  \"files.associations\": {\n    \"*.sql\": \"smelt\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Key Patterns for Writing New Tests\n\n**Pattern 1: Basic test structure**\n```typescript\nlet server: CodeServerHandle;\n\ntest.beforeAll(async () => {\n  if (!process.env.CODE_SERVER_URL) {\n    server = await launchCodeServer();\n  }\n});\n\ntest.afterAll(async () => {\n  server?.stop();\n});\n\ntest(\"description\", async ({ page }) => {\n  const url = process.env.CODE_SERVER_URL ?? server.url;\n  await page.goto(url, { waitUntil: \"load\" });\n  await waitForWorkbench(page);\n  await dismissDialogs(page);\n  // Test logic...\n});\n```\n\n**Pattern 2: Wait for LSP initialization**\n- Use `waitForLSPReady(page, { timeout })` for reliable LSP detection\n- Or `waitForDiagnostics(page, { timeout })` if LSP produces errors on a known-broken file\n\n**Pattern 3: Interact with editor**\n- `openFile(page, \"path/to/file.sql\")` - opens via Ctrl+P\n- `goToLine(page, N)` - positions cursor\n- `hoverWord(page, \"word\", { line })` - triggers hover\n\n**Pattern 4: Screenshot for documentation**\n- `screenshot(page, { feature: \"name\", name: \"step\" })` - saves to `docs/demos/media/name/step.png`\n- `screenshotEditor()` - just editor area, better for tight docs\n- `screenshotWithOverlay()` - captures hover/menu overlays\n\n**Pattern 5: Assert LSP behavior**\n- Count squigglies: `page.locator(\".squiggly-error\").count()`\n- Check specific diagnostics via hover widget content\n\nAll files are ready for you to write new tests following these exact patterns!"}],"totalDurationMs":35962,"totalTokens":32201,"totalToolUseCount":19,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1712,"cache_read_input_tokens":26742,"output_tokens":3740,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1712},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
